# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
# Summary: macOS CLI lists on-screen application windows via Core Graphics, filters layer-0 rows with dedupe, emits JSON report envelope on stdout.

## LIST_ON_SCREEN_WINDOWS
# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
# How: Darwin cgo path calls CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo with on-screen and exclude-desktop flags; maps CF rows to RawWindowRecord with top-left bounds.

# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
Contract:
  INPUT: none
  OUTPUT: []RawWindowRecord pre-filter CG rows
  DATA: primary_display_height for bounds transform
  CONTROL: darwin build tag only; !darwin returns clear error
  PRE: GOOS == darwin; Core Graphics APIs available
  POST: every record has window_id, owner_name, owner_pid, layer, bounds (top-left origin), title (may be empty string), is_onscreen
  EFFECTS: calls CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo; CFRelease on window array
  FAILURE_MODES: CG_CALL_FAILED — return error; no partial records; stdout must remain empty on failure path
  DATA_TRANSITION: CFArray → []RawWindowRecord
  TERMINATION: total — single CG query per invocation

# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
# How: Query CG for on-screen windows excluding desktop elements; extract fields; transform bounds to top-left origin.
procedure LIST_ON_SCREEN_WINDOWS:
  IF runtime.GOOS != "darwin":
    RETURN error("desktop window report requires macOS")
  options := kCGWindowListOptionOnScreenOnly | kCGWindowListExcludeDesktopElements
  cfArray := CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo(options, kCGNullWindowID)
  IF cfArray == nil:
    RETURN error("CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo failed")
  DEFER CFRelease(cfArray)
  primaryHeight := primaryDisplayHeight()
  rawRecords := empty slice
  FOR each dict IN cfArray:
    APPEND mapCGRow(dict, primaryHeight) TO rawRecords
  RETURN rawRecords, nil

## FILTER_APPLICATION_WINDOWS
# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
# How: Pure Go filter keeps layer == 0 only; dedupe by window_id preferring is_onscreen == true.

# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
Contract:
  INPUT: []RawWindowRecord
  OUTPUT: []WindowRecord deduplicated application windows
  DATA: dedupe map keyed by window_id
  CONTROL: pure Go; no cgo
  PRE: input slice non-nil (empty allowed)
  POST: no duplicate window_id; all layer == 0; title key always present (empty string allowed)
  EFFECTS: none external
  FAILURE_MODES: none — empty input yields empty output
  DATA_TRANSITION: []RawWindowRecord → []WindowRecord
  TERMINATION: total — single pass with dedupe merge

# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
# How: Exclude non-layer-0 rows; group by window_id; when colliding prefer is_onscreen true; emit WindowRecord slice.
procedure FILTER_APPLICATION_WINDOWS:
  dedupe := empty map window_id → RawWindowRecord
  FOR each raw IN input:
    IF raw.layer != 0:
      CONTINUE
    IF existing, ok := dedupe[raw.window_id]; ok:
      IF raw.is_onscreen AND NOT existing.is_onscreen:
        dedupe[raw.window_id] = raw
      CONTINUE
    dedupe[raw.window_id] = raw
  out := empty []WindowRecord
  FOR each kept IN dedupe:
    APPEND WindowRecord from kept TO out
  RETURN out

## EMIT_JSON_REPORT
# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
# How: Build Report envelope with UTC RFC3339 reported_at, platform darwin, windows slice, count; encode to stdout.

# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
Contract:
  INPUT: []WindowRecord filtered windows
  OUTPUT: JSON bytes on stdout
  DATA: Report envelope
  CONTROL: exit 0 on success; exit 1 on marshal failure
  PRE: filtered windows available (empty slice allowed)
  POST: valid JSON; count == len(windows); all contract keys present including empty title
  EFFECTS: writes stdout; sets exit 0
  FAILURE_MODES: JSON_MARSHAL_FAILED — message on stderr; exit 1; stdout empty
  DATA_TRANSITION: []WindowRecord → Report → JSON
  TERMINATION: total — single encode

# [IMPL-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [ARCH-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT] [REQ-DESKTOP_WINDOW_REPORT]
# How: Assemble envelope and json.Encode to stdout via CLI main.
procedure EMIT_JSON_REPORT:
  report := Report{
    reported_at: time.Now().UTC().Format(RFC3339),
    platform: "darwin",
    windows: input,
    count: len(input),
  }
  bytes := json.Marshal(report)
  IF marshal error:
    WRITE error to stderr
    EXIT 1
  WRITE bytes to stdout
  EXIT 0
